 * Optional helper: builds the Google Forms in forms/*.md from spec/forms.json, so the per-campaign
 * survey takes one click instead of ten minutes. The manual steps in forms/survey-form.md are the
 * fallback and say exactly the same thing.
 *
 * UNVERIFIED AGAINST GOOGLE: written to Google's documented FormApp, SpreadsheetApp and DriveApp
 * methods and tested only against a local mock (tests/test_forms_gs.js). Run it once on a test
 * campaign and compare the form with forms/survey-form.md before relying on it.
 *
 * Install [FOUNDER LOGIN: Google]: in the tracker, Extensions > Apps Script > new file
 * "build-forms", paste this whole file, save. Run from the editor:
 *   buildMasters()                 once: the survey and newsletter masters, and the two founder-side intake forms
 *                                  (the intake forms are linked to this spreadsheet; rename their tabs office_form and brand_form)
 *   makeCampaignSurvey("CMP-003")  at T-4: that campaign's survey (and sign-up form if newsletter_option = Y);
 *                                  links the survey here, renames its tab to the campaign_id, and writes
 *                                  survey_form_url, survey_prefill_template and newsletter_form_url on the campaigns tab
 * Nothing is sent or shared. Forms are created in your Drive with names that never contain the company name.
 * Generated by tools/make_forms_gs.py from spec/forms.json. Do not edit SPEC by hand.
 */

